{"nodes": [{"id": "claude_doc", "label": "CLAUDE.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_springengine", "label": "SpringEngine", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_maven_scaffold", "label": "Maven scaffold (pom.xml template)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_spring_test_code_field", "label": "spring_test_code field", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_executionengine_run_exercise_param", "label": "ExecutionEngine.run() exercise parameter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "ExecutionEngine.run() gained an optional exercise: Optional[Exercise] = None keyword param because a Spring exercise isn't a single self-contained code string the way Python/Java/C++ are -- SpringEngine needs it to look up the exercise's fixed spring_test_code. Unused by the three single-file engines; lesson_screen.py passes it on every call regardless of language, so only SpringEngine needed to change behavior when it was added."}, {"id": "concept_build_success_synthetic_stdout", "label": "BUILD SUCCESS synthetic stdout", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Maven's own logger writes everything, including [ERROR] diagnostics, to stdout (never stderr) -- SpringEngine routes that into ExecutionResult.stderr on failure to match the other engines' contract, and returns a synthetic, deterministic stdout=\"BUILD SUCCESS\" on success rather than the real surefire summary line, since that line's elapsed-time/class-name content is non-deterministic and can't reliably satisfy validate_output()'s re.fullmatch(). Every Spring exercise's expected_output_pattern is accordingly just \"BUILD SUCCESS\"."}, {"id": "concept_sanitize_path", "label": "_sanitize_path() (temp dir path stripping)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "concept_spring_friendly_errors", "label": "Spring friendly error translation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_execution_base_executionengine", "label": "ExecutionEngine (ABC, code)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_execution_base_executionengine_run", "label": "ExecutionEngine.run() (code)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_execution_spring_engine_springengine", "label": "SpringEngine (code)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_execution_spring_engine__sanitize_path", "label": "_sanitize_path() (code)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "app_execution_errors_translate_spring_error", "label": "_translate_spring_error() (code)", "file_type": "code", "source_file": "CLAUDE.md"